  "description": "The 2026 Colorado gubernatorial election is an open-seat race to succeed term-limited Democratic Governor Jared Polis, who is ineligible to seek a third consecutive term. Candidates are competing in primary elections on June 30, 2026, with the general election on November 3, 2026. Democrats have won every gubernatorial election in Colorado since 2006 and the state has voted Democratic in every presidential election since 2008, giving the Democratic nominees a structural advantage. The Democratic primary features U.S. Senator Michael Bennet and state Attorney General Phil Weiser, while the Republican primary includes state Representative Scott Bottoms, state Senator Barbara Kirkmeyer, and Marine veteran/minister Victor Marx.",
